    "ABAWD is the official name for these work rules. Hiraku does not determine your eligibility or case status.": "ABAWD 是這些工作規定的官方名稱。Hiraku 不決定您的資格或案件狀態。",
    "ACCESS NYC’s preparation guidance": "ACCESS NYC 的準備指南",
    "Add the household’s monthly income from work and other sources, such as unemployment, Social Security, and child support received. Gross means before taxes or paycheck deductions: if a pay stub shows $1,500 before tax and $1,250 take-home, use $1,500. Use a monthly total, not one week’s pay. If you’re unsure which income to count, including self-employment or boarder income, choose I don’t know.": "請加入家庭從工作和其他來源（例如失業救濟金、社會安全金和收到的撫養費）獲得的每月收入。總收入是指扣除稅款或薪資扣除額之前的金額：如果薪資單顯示稅前 $1,500 且實領 $1,250，請使用 $1,500。請使用每月總額，而不是一週的薪水。如果您不確定要計算哪些收入（包括自營工作或房客收入），請選擇「我不知道」。",
    "Adjust or clear your radius to search again.": "調整或清除您的搜尋半徑以再次搜尋。",
    "After subtracting child support paid, your monthly gross income of {income} is above the {limit} guideline for your household size.": "扣除支付的撫養費後，您每月 {income} 的總收入高於您家庭人數規定的 {limit} 標準。",
    "After subtracting child support paid, your monthly gross income of {income} is at or below the {limit} guideline for your household size.": "扣除已支付的赡养费後，您家庭规模的每月总收入 {income} 等于或低于 {limit} 指南。",
    "Already applied or receiving SNAP? These links take you to official services for your case.": "已經申請或正在接收 SNAP？這些連結將帶您前往您案件的官方服務。",
    "Answer a few questions to check a limited income guideline and understand what to do next. This is for NYC residents who haven’t applied.": "回答幾個問題以檢查有限的收入標準並了解接下來該怎麼做。這是給尚未申請的紐約市居民準備的。",
    "Apply on ACCESS HRA (optional) ↗": "在 ACCESS HRA 上申請（選填） ↗",
    "Approximate proximity, not route distance.": "大約的鄰近距離，並非行車距離。",
    "Ask Shosai": "詢問 Shosai",
    "Ask a question between 1 and 2,000 characters.": "請提出一個介於 1 到 2,000 字元之間的問題。",
    "Ask about an exemption or how to document approved activities. After three countable months, benefits can stop or be reduced again.": "詢問豁免或如何記錄獲批准的活動。在計算滿三個月後，福利可能會再次停止或減少。",
    "Ask general questions about SNAP rules, including income. Shosai can explain NYC guidance but cannot assess your eligibility or estimate benefits. If you want to check your own situation, use Hiraku’s screener or apply through NYC HRA.": "提出關於 SNAP 規則（包括收入）的一般問題。Shosai 可以解釋紐約市的指引，但無法評估您的資格或估算福利。如果您想檢查自己的情況，請使用 Hiraku 的篩選工具或透過 NYC HRA 申請。",
